{% set local_problem %}
<p>Decatur's river location creates perfect conditions for fascia damage — and we see it constantly when inspecting homes here. Tennessee River keeps humidity levels 10-15% higher in Decatur than areas just a short drive inland. That constantly moist air surrounds your home 365 days a year, and exposed wood pays the price.</p>

<p>Here's what happens: gutters clog or overflow during a storm. Water runs behind the gutter and soaks into the fascia board. In a drier climate, that wood might dry within a day or two. In Decatur's humidity, it stays damp much longer — sometimes never fully drying between rain events during wet seasons. That persistent moisture is exactly what rot fungus needs to thrive.</p>

<p>We see fascia damage across every <a href="/recent-projects/">Decatur neighborhood</a>. Historic homes in Albany and downtown often have original wood fascia weathered by decades of river-town humidity. Mid-century homes throughout the city frequently show multiple repair attempts over the years. Even newer construction in Southwest Decatur exhibits accelerated wear compared to homes in drier areas just 20 miles away.</p>

<p>The damage often goes unnoticed until it's extensive. Fascia boards hide behind your gutters, out of sight. Paint may look fine from the ground while the wood underneath is rotting through. Many homeowners discover the problem only when gutters start sagging or pulling away.</p>

<p><strong>The uncomfortable truth:</strong> About 50% of gutter replacement jobs in Decatur also need some fascia work. Not the whole house — usually isolated sections where gutters leaked or overflowed consistently. In drier areas, that number is closer to 30-40%. River-town humidity makes the difference. We'd rather tell you upfront than install new gutters on compromised wood.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>We start with thorough inspection — checking fascia and soffit for water damage, soft spots, and rot. In Decatur's humidity, we pay special attention to hidden areas: behind gutter brackets, at corners where water collects, and where fascia meets soffit. Damage often isn't visible until you actually press on the wood.</p>

<p><strong>For damaged sections:</strong> We carefully remove existing gutters, cut out rotted wood back to solid material, and install new fascia boards. Given Decatur's humidity, we typically recommend moisture-resistant materials: composite boards rated for ground contact, treated lumber, or PVC-wrapped options that stand up better to river-town climate.</p>

<p><strong>Material choice matters here:</strong> Standard pine fascia lasts maybe 8-10 years in Decatur before showing moisture damage. Composite or treated lumber lasts 20+ years. The upgrade costs 30-40% more but more than doubles the lifespan. In this humidity, it's worth it.</p>

<p>Everything gets properly sealed, caulked, and prepped for new gutter installation. We use primers and sealants designed for humid conditions — not generic products that break down quickly in moisture-heavy environments.</p>

<p>Then we install your new seamless gutters on the fresh fascia — properly attached with hangers at 24-inch intervals, properly sloped for drainage, designed to prevent the overflow that caused the rot originally. One contractor handling everything: carpentry, gutters, proper coordination, single warranty.</p>

<p><strong>What we won't do:</strong> Slap new gutters on damaged fascia just to close the sale. Some gutter companies ignore fascia problems because they don't do carpentry. We'd rather lose a job than install gutters we know won't last.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've repaired fascia and installed gutters throughout <a href="/recent-projects/">Morgan County</a> for over 20 years. We understand these jobs are inseparable — you can't have reliable gutters without solid fascia to mount them, and you can't protect fascia without properly functioning gutters keeping water away from it.</p>

<p>We also understand what Decatur's humidity does to exposed wood. Our material recommendations, installation techniques, and attention to moisture management are specifically designed for river-town conditions — not generic solutions from a franchise playbook.</p>

<p>Our crews handle both carpentry and gutter installation. Better coordination, cleaner work, single point of accountability. When we're done, your home is protected from roof edge to foundation — backed by our warranty and our 20+ year reputation in Morgan County.</p>

<p><strong>Warning from experience:</strong> If someone offers to install new gutters and says your fascia "looks fine" without actually getting up there and pressing on it, get a second opinion. We've replaced plenty of gutters installed 2-3 years ago on damaged fascia — the original installer either didn't notice or didn't mention it. Now the homeowner pays twice.</p>

<p><strong>Our advice:</strong> If you're replacing gutters in Decatur and your existing ones have leaked for years, expect some fascia damage. It's just the reality of river-town living. Better to know about it and fix it now than discover it when your new gutters start sagging in 18 months.</p>
{% endset %}

